Spec: LibBackupContext

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Build the restic backup/restore ENV and CONTEXT consumed by the service and tenant
    backup/restore lanes, in two disjoint halves. @from_args(context) reads the
    backup/restore Pod's own process environment (repo URL, snapshot, engine lists,
    retention, scale, TLS) back into the args map the runtime stages use; @run(instance,
    context, use_init_from) produces that environment on the other side, assembling the
    volumes/mounts/env/envFrom/files/CronJob fields of the init, schedule and
    backup/restore pods that the ./../service and ./../tenant lane templates render.

Exposes:
  @from_args(context) — env→map half; reached as `ctx::from_args(args)` by
    ./../service/backup.rhai, ./../service/restore.rhai, ./../tenant/backup.rhai,
    ./../tenant/restore.rhai. Mutates the passed map in place and returns it; reads no
    key of it (only its own just-written values), overwrites exactly the 19 keys
    `deployment_list`, `statefulset_list`, `secret_list`, `pg_list`, `mysql_list`,
    `mongo_list`, `redis_list`, `restic_tags`, `snapshot`, `max_dayly`, `max_weekly`,
    `max_monthly`, `max_yearly`, `namespace`, `scale_target`, `sub_path`, `base_path`,
    `s3_url`, `restic_args`.
  @run(instance, context, use_init_from) — map→env half; reached as
    `bctx::run(instance, context, true)` by ./../service/init_from.rhai and its tenant
    twin (restore-from-instance lane feeding `{{> init_job.yaml }}`), and with `false`
    as the third arg by ./../service/schedule_backup.rhai and its tenant twin (feeding
    `{{> cronbackup.yaml }}`). Mutates and returns the same @context map; overwrites the
    keys `volumes`, `mounts`, `envs_from`, `envs`, `files`, `has_files`, `schedule`,
    `service_account`, `backup_affinity`.
  The two fns share no keys: no env key written by @run equals a context key @from_args
    reads — the coupling is env-NAME-level through the rendered pod spec (see `Must`).
  Importing the module runs nothing: the file body is one `//` comment and the two @fn
    definitions, zero executable top-level code, so @import_run / @import on
    `backup_context` touch no env, no filesystem and no cluster.

Accepts:
  @from_args @context — any @rhai map used as accumulator (callers pass the ten-key CLI
    `args` map injected by the Rust lane). All inputs are @get_env reads:
    `DEPLOYMENT_LIST`, `STATEFULSET_LIST`, `SECRET_LIST`, `PG_LIST`, `MYSQL_LIST`,
    `MONGO_LIST`, `REDIS_LIST` (space-separated -> arrays); `RESTIC_TAGS`,
    `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT`, `NAMESPACE`, `SUB_PATH`, `BASE_REPO_URL` (raw strings);
    `RESTIC_MAX_DAYLY`/`RESTIC_MAX_WEEKLY`/`RESTIC_MAX_MONTHLY`/`RESTIC_MAX_YEARLY`
    (empty -> `7`/`5`/`12`/`4` respectively); `SCALE_TARGET` (@parse_int, any rejected
    text -> int `1`, negatives kept); `INSECURE_TLS` (`== "true"` exact only).
  @run @instance — a @ServiceInstance/@TenantInstance @Dynamic exposing
    `.status.vitals` (REQUIRED array of `#{name, kind}`), `.status.scalables`
    (nullable — guarded `!= ()`), and, only when @use_init_from, `.spec.initFrom`
    (`.secretName`, `.subPath`, `.snapshot`, each separately nullable via `!= ()`).
  @run @context — the install-lane context map: must carry `instance` (`name`,
    `namespace`, `appslug`, `requested` and `["package"].name/.type/.backup_affinity`),
    `namespace` (map: `ha`, `maintenance_start_minut`, `maintenance_start_hour` — the
    `minut` misspelling is the cross-script contract), `cluster.vynil_namespace`,
    `agent_image`, `package_dir`; and `tenant.name` additionally when
    `["package"].type == "tenant"` — missing scalar map keys read as `()` and
    interpolate as `()`, missing intermediate maps raise on the next dot.
  @use_init_from — boolean flag positional third arg.

Returns:
  Both fns return the SAME mutated map passed in (last-expression `context`).
  @from_args arrays are @Array of @String (empty env -> empty array: `"".split(" ")`
    then @filter drops the single empty piece); `scale_target` is an int, retention and
    snapshot values stay env strings; `s3_url` is `s3:${base_path}/${sub_path}`;
    `restic_args` is `""` or `" --insecure-tls"` (leading space present).
  @run writes `envs_from` as one secretRef entry (name `backup-settings` unless
    initFrom overrides — that Secret must supply the restic repo credentials via envFrom),
    `has_files` boolean, `schedule` cron text `${maintenance_start_minut} ${maintenance_start_hour} * * *`,
    `service_account` `${appslug}-backup`, `backup_affinity` copied verbatim from
    `instance["package"].backup_affinity` (may be `()`, not filtered).

Raises:
  @from_args raises nothing for any env state (@get_env answers `""` unset, @parse_int
    failure is caught); it raises only if @context is not a map (index-assign miss).
  @run has zero @throw — failures are raw engine raises escaping unguarded spots:
    `.status.vitals` absent or non-array (the `for` over `()`), any property dot on a
    `()` intermediate (`instance` key missing, or `use_init_from` true while
    `.spec.initFrom` itself is absent), `@file_read` inside the scripts scan, and the
    Cluster branch's `k8s_resource("Secret", ns).@list_meta()` cluster call — that one
    cluster read sits OUTSIDE any @try, so a Secrets-list failure aborts the whole run.
  The MariaDB/NdbCluster/MongoDBCommunity/Dragonfly/RedisCluster/RedisSentinel branches
    each wrap their CR @get in @try/@catch: a raised string is @log_warn'ed as-is,
    anything else through @json_encode, and the branch is skipped (engine stays out of
    its list). See Tasks: @json_encode of a non-serializable caught payload can itself
    raise out of the @catch and still abort the run.
  Absence-not-guarded spots: every `context.<key>.<field>` second-level dot; guarded
    spots: the six DB/redis CR reads, `users[0]` (guarded by `users.len() > 0` — though a
    missing `users[0].connectionStringSecretName` reads `()` and is written into the
    `secretKeyRef.name` unvalidated), the per-list `.reduce` (guarded `len() > 0`, and
    the rhai seed-free `reduce` starts the accumulator at `()` and returns `()` on
    empty, which is why every reducer tests `sum.type_of() == "()"` first).

Handles:
  Two disjoint lanes per import (runtime Pod from env / producer for pod specs) —
    described in `Exposes`; neither fn calls the other.
  Engine dispatch is by @v.kind string on `instance.status.vitals`:
    `PersistentVolumeClaim`, `Secret`, `Cluster`, `MariaDB`, `NdbCluster`,
    `MongoDBCommunity`, `Dragonfly`, `RedisCluster`, `RedisSentinel`; any other kind is
    ignored. `instance.status.scalables` `Deployment`/`StatefulSet` names feed
    `DEPLOYMENT_LIST`/`STATEFULSET_LIST`.
  Per-vital name sanitize (in place — rhai @replace/@trim mutate their @ImmutableString
    receiver): strip every occurrence of `appslug`, swap `-`/space, @trim, restore `-`;
    the empty result selects a per-kind default volume/suffix name — `data` (PVC),
    `secret`, `postgres` (Cluster), `mariadb`, `ndb`, `mongodb`, `dragonfly`, `redis`
    (both RedisCluster and RedisSentinel).
  Secret vitals always contribute env `secret_${name}_target` (value = raw vital name)
    and the `SECRET_LIST` entry; their `/secrets/${name}` volume+mount are written only
    when @use_init_from is false (init-from pods get secret values through
    the initFrom Secret instead).
  Per-engine env blocks (all under the sanitized `${name}_` prefix):
    Cluster/pgs — secret picked as `${v.name}-superuser` when the Secret @list_meta
    filter finds it, else `${v.name}-app`; keys `host`, `username`, `password`,
    `dbname` ALL written as `valueFrom.secretKeyRef` (host included, from the secret).
    MariaDB — root leg when `spec.rootPasswordSecretKeyRef.name` present: literal `root`
    username, password key ref (key `?? "password"`), literal host
    `${v.name}.${namespace}.svc`, dbname literal with `?? "*"` fallback to the string
    `"*"`; else user leg
    (needs password ref + username + dbname all non-`()`): literal username, same
    password/host shape, literal dbname. Absent either leg: warn-free silent skip.
    NdbCluster — needs `spec.mysqlNode.rootPasswordSecretName`; refs keys
    `username`/`password`, host `${v.name}-mysqld.${namespace}.svc`, dbname `"*"`.
    MongoDBCommunity — needs `spec.users[0].connectionStringSecretName`; refs keys
    `username`/`password`, host `${v.name}-svc.${namespace}.svc`, dbname `"*"`.
    Dragonfly — needs `spec.authentication.passwordFromSecret.name`; password ref,
    literal host `${v.name}.${namespace}.svc`, plus `${name}_kind` = `"Dragonfly"` and
    `${name}_sts` = raw vital name. RedisCluster — `spec.kubernetesConfig.redisSecret`,
    host `${v.name}-leader...`, `_sts` `${v.name}-leader`; RedisSentinel — same secret
    path, host `${v.name}-master...`, `_sts` `${v.name}-master`. Redis engines get
    `password`-only refs (no username/dbname keys). The optional password `key` defaults
    to `"password"` via `??` on both mariadb refs and all three redis secret reads.
  The `${name}.*` and secret-target env names are generated independently per vital;
    two vitals sanitizing to the same name produce duplicate env entries, undeclared
    here (see Tasks).
  Scripts scan: `@is_dir(`${package_dir}/scripts`)` then @read_dir, keeping files whose
    @basename @starts_with `backup`, `restore` or `maintenance` as
    `#{name, content}` via @file_read; `has_files` additionally appends a configMap
    volume `${appslug}-backups-scripts` (`defaultMode: 493` = 0755) mounted at
    `/package/scripts` beside the always-present `empty-dir` volume mounted at
    `/backup`; PVCs mount at `/backup/${name}`, secrets at `/secrets/${name}`.

Must:
  List envs `DEPLOYMENT_LIST`, `STATEFULSET_LIST`, `PG_LIST`, `MYSQL_LIST`, `MONGO_LIST`,
    `REDIS_LIST`, `SECRET_LIST` are emitted ONLY when non-empty, joined space-separated
    by the `()`-seeded @reduce idiom — empty lists emit no env name at all.
  Emit the @envs base list in this fixed shape: `RESTIC_TAGS`, `RESTIC_HOST` (=
    appslug), `GOMAXPROCS` = `"2"`, `GOMEMLIMIT` = `"1560MiB"`, `GOGC` = `"50"`,
    `AGENT_IMAGE` (from context), `SCALE_TARGET` = `"2"` when `context.namespace.ha`
    else `"1"`, `VYNIL_NAMESPACE` (from `context.cluster.vynil_namespace`), `INSTANCE`,
    `TAG` (= `instance.requested`), `SUB_PATH` (= `${instance.namespace}/${appslug}` by
    default, initFrom.subPath wins), `APPSLUG`, then `NAMESPACE` and `POD_NAME` as
    `valueFrom.fieldRef` downward-API entries (`metadata.namespace` / `metadata.name`) —
    the two and the DB password/host refs are the only non-literal-value entries.
  `RESTIC_TAGS` composes as
    `namespace:${ns},instance:${name},component:${package.name},version:${requested}`
    plus `,tenant:${context.tenant.name}` appended if and only if
    `package.type == "tenant"`.
  Append `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT` (value `instance.spec.initFrom.snapshot`, possibly `()`
    when that key is absent — the entry is NOT skipped) only when @use_init_from is
    true; the schedule lane therefore never carries it.
  Run @sub_path/base_path normalization in @from_args, not in @run: the
    `@replace("/"," ")` -> @trim -> `@replace(" ","/")` in-place chain strips leading
    and trailing slashes/whitespace of SUB_PATH and BASE_REPO_URL (interior
    double-slashes survive, interior spaces become `/`); run's own default/defaulted
    `SUB_PATH` env gets no such treatment.
  Read BASE_REPO_URL/SUB_PATH normalized into key `s3_url` as
    `s3:${base_path}/${sub_path}` — with unset env degrading to `s3:/`.
  Keep the retention defaults as STRINGS `"7"`, `"5"`, `"12"`, `"4"` for
    `max_dayly`/`max_weekly`/`max_monthly`/`max_yearly` (only when the env is empty;
    the `dayly` misspelling matches the env name `RESTIC_MAX_DAYLY`).

Depends on:
  Wynil-core 0.7.7 registrars behind the @Script::new live engine
    (./../../../common/src/rhaihandler.sdd) and the @Script::new_mock test engines — the
    script just calls the registered names: @get_env, @log_warn, @json_encode, @basename
    (`core_common_rhai_register`), @is_dir, @read_dir, @file_read (`fs_rhai_register`,
    `fs` feature), @k8s_resource(name, ns)/@get/@list_meta on the `"K8sGeneric"` type
    (`k8sgeneric_rhai_register` — `.list_meta()` is the metadata-only variant, and the
    `k8sraw` `get_url` surface is not used here), @parse_int and the map/reduce/
    filter/@trim/@replace builtins. Spec boundary ends at "the script calls X".
  ./../service/backup.rhai, ./../service/restore.rhai, ./../tenant/backup.rhai,
    ./../tenant/restore.rhai — @from_args(`args`) callers (alias `ctx`);
    ./../service/init_from.rhai, ./../tenant/init_from.rhai — @run(..., true);
    ./../service/schedule_backup.rhai, ./../tenant/schedule_backup.rhai — @run(...,
    false) inside a @try whose @catch reports via `set_status_schedule_backup_failed`
    then re-throws.
  /agent/src/service/backup.sdd, /agent/src/service/restore.sdd,
    /agent/src/tenant/backup.sdd, /agent/src/tenant/restore.sdd — the Rust-lane specs
    that froze the consumer-side env contract this file's @from_args half satisfies
    (reconciled in the `from_args` accept list; drifts in Tasks).
  /agent/tests/rhai_lib.rs — the only tests naming this module (five pattern-simulating
    `eval` snippets on `make_lib_script()`, a mock engine over `scripts/lib` only — none
    calls either fn).

Scenario: from_args full environment decodes
  Given process env with `DEPLOYMENT_LIST="a b"`, `PG_LIST="pg main"`,
    `RESTIC_MAX_DAYLY="3"`, `SCALE_TARGET="10"`, `INSECURE_TLS="true"`,
    `BASE_REPO_URL="https://repo/"`, `SUB_PATH="/ns/app/"` and the rest empty
  When @from_args runs on an empty map
  Then `deployment_list` = `["a","b"]` (empty inner pieces filtered), `pg_list` has both
    names, `max_dayly` is `"3"` while `max_weekly`/`max_monthly`/`max_yearly` fall to
    `"5"`/`"12"`/`"4"`
  And `scale_target` is the int `10`, `restic_args` is `" --insecure-tls"`, and both
    paths lost their edge slashes so `s3_url` is `s3:https://repo/ns/app`

Scenario: from_args on a bare environment
  Given every read env var unset (each @get_env answers `""`)
  When @from_args runs
  Then every list key is an empty @Array, `snapshot` and `restic_tags` are `""`, the four
    retention keys are `"7"`/`"5"`, `"12"`, `"4"`, `scale_target` is int `1` (the
    @parse_int `""` throw is caught), `restic_args` keeps `""`, `s3_url` is the degraded
    `s3:/` — no raise anywhere

Scenario: run secret and PVC mounting split by lane
  Given a context with `instance` (`appslug: "box-shop"`) plus package type `service`,
    and a `status.vitals` of one @PersistentVolumeClaim and one @Secret
  When @run is called with @use_init_from false
  Then `volumes`/`mounts` carry the `empty-dir` pair, a PVC volume named from the
    sanitized vital (default `data` when the name sanitizes empty) mounted at
    `/backup/${name}`, and the Secret volume at `/secrets/${name}`
  And `envs` holds `secret_${name}_target` with the raw vital name and `SECRET_LIST`
    with that name, while `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT` is absent and `has_files` reflects the
    scripts scan

Scenario: run init-from overrides
  Given the same with `use_init_from` true and `instance.spec.initFrom` carrying
    `secretName`, `subPath` and `snapshot`
  When @run runs
  Then `envs_from` names the initFrom Secret instead of `backup-settings`, `SUB_PATH`
    takes the initFrom subPath, `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT` is appended with the initFrom snapshot,
    and the Secret vital contributes env + `SECRET_LIST` but NO `/secrets/` volume

Scenario: engine pick and skip-by-absence
  Given vitals with a CNPG `Cluster` named `db` while a Secret `db-superuser` exists in
    the @list_meta result, one @MariaDB whose CR exposes only
    `rootPasswordSecretKeyRef`, one @RedisSentinel with `kubernetesConfig.redisSecret`
  When @run runs
  Then the `db_host`/`db_username`/`db_password`/`db_dbname` envs (sanitized-vital
    prefix) all index secret `db-superuser` on keys
    `host`/`username`/`password`/`dbname` (host included), `MYSQL_LIST` names the
    sanitized mariadb whose username env is the literal `root`, and `REDIS_LIST` plus
    `_kind` = `"RedisSentinel"` / `_sts` suffix `-master` are set
  But a mariadb vital whose CR @get raises (or has neither credential leg) is only
    @log_warn'd/ignored and stays out of `MYSQL_LIST`

Scenario: scripts scan feeds the configMap pair
  Given `${package_dir}/scripts` containing `backup.sh`, `maintenance_stop.sh` and
    `other.sh`
  When @run runs
  Then `files` holds `#{name: "backup.sh", ...}` and the maintenance entry (content =
    full file text) but not `other.sh`, `has_files` is true, and `volumes`/`mounts` gain
    `${appslug}-backups-scripts` at `/package/scripts`

Scenario: the unguarded cluster read and dead vitals abort
  Given vitals including a `Cluster` vital while the Secret @list_meta call fails, or a
    context where the `instance` key is missing, or `status` without `vitals`
  When @run runs
  Then each of the three raises out of the function (Cluster-list failure is outside any
    @try; the last two are property-on-`()` raises) — the schedule lane sees them as its
    own @catch status-failure text

Example:
  `RESTIC_TAGS` full form: `namespace:web,instance:shop,component:shop-pkg,version:1.4.2`
    plus `,tenant:acme` on tenant packages
  from_args key/value types: lists `Array<String>`, `scale_target` int, `restic_args`
    `" --insecure-tls"` or `""`

Tasks:
  [ ] Call @from_args directly from /agent/tests/rhai_lib.rs: no test invokes either fn.
      The five existing `backup_context_*` tests @eval hand-copied pattern snippets
      (split/filter, seeded reduce incl. the `()`-seed idiom, both replace/trim chains)
      and would keep passing even if this module deleted; /agent/tests/rhai_backup_redis.rs
      never names this file. Drive from_args with `@std::env` fixtures once injectable,
      and @run through `make_lib_script_with_k8s` mocks covering the nine kinds, both
      init_from legs, the scripts scan and each @catch.
  [?] Produce/consume drift toward the four Rust-lane specs: @from_args reads
      `BASE_REPO_URL`, `SUB_PATH`, `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT`, `NAMESPACE`, both list sets and the
      retention/scale/TLS envs, but @run WRITES NO `BASE_REPO_URL`, NO
      `INSECURE_TLS` and NO `RESTIC_MAX_*` entry — those five (plus
      `NAMESPACE` as plain string, which the restore.sdd env enumeration also omits) have
      no producer anywhere in this file, and the specs only say unset envs resolve to
      empty by @get_env, silently degrading `s3_url` to `s3:/`. Confirm the operator/box
      Job env is their real producer and settle which side freezes them.
  [?] Consumer-side list for the @run-only envs: `RESTIC_HOST` (restic binary),
      `GOMAXPROCS`/`GOMEMLIMIT`/`GOGC` (Go tuning constants baked here),
      `AGENT_IMAGE`/`INSTANCE`/`TAG`/`VYNIL_NAMESPACE`/`APPSLUG`/`POD_NAME`, the
      `secret_*_target` and `${name}_host/_username/_password/_dbname/_kind/_sts`
      families are read by the package scripts and stage modules via shell env, not by
      @from_args, and no spec yet freezes which reader takes which — enumerate here or
      move each to its owner once the stage scripts get specs.
  [?] Duplicate generated env names: two vitals sanitizing to the same `${name}` (e.g.
      two Clusters, or a Secret and a Cluster both reducing to `main`) emit colliding
      env entries and volumes with no detection — decide whether the file must
      disambiguate or the CR surface forbids it.
  [?] Name sanitize removes EVERY appslug occurrence, not just the prefix, and turns
      interior spaces into `-` — decide whether prefix-strip is the intent (the
      existing simulate-only test only exercises the prefix case).
  [?] initFrom with `snapshot` absent still appends `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT` with a `()` value
      into the rendered pod spec, while the schedule lane never sets the name at all —
      confirm the `()`-valued env entry is tolerated by the init_job template or must be
      guarded like the retention defaults.
  [?] Inside the six DB/redis @catch blocks, @json_encode(e) on a non-serializable
      caught payload would itself raise and abort @run — decide whether the catch must
      degrade to a lossier log, and pin with a mock @get failure what @type_of the
      raised system errors actually report (the `"string"` arm only covers thrown
      strings).
  [?] `context["namespace"]` is a plain string in the @from_args lane but a map
      (`ha`/maintenance fields) in the template lane — same key, two types, never in one
      map today; confirm the split stays or rename one side.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a mapped @Script::new_mock test against this module (not a copied
    snippet), the produce/consume env contract with the four Rust-lane specs is closed on
    whichever side owns each var, and `specdd lint` stays green.
